msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:117 455dea23c7844f53bcb08f865a45b406
msgid ""
"Get UniProt-to-PDB chain mappings for a PDB structure from the PDBe Graph"
" API. For each UniProt a..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst 0e2bbee204bd47199bb42cefb4c6886a
msgid "PDBe_get_uniprot_mappings tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:123 b5797619bb894ea282390671acb30960
msgid "**Name**: ``PDBe_get_uniprot_mappings``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:125 54867de23649481eab7366c9bf35da5b
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get UniProt-to-PDB chain mappings for a PDB structure "
"from the PDBe Graph API. For each UniProt accession represented in the "
"structure, returns all chain mappings with residue-level alignment "
"(UniProt start/end, PDB start/end, identity, coverage). Essential for "
"understanding which proteins are in a crystal structure and how they map "
"to UniProt reference sequences. Example: 4HHB returns P69905 "
"(HBA\\_HUMAN) mapped to chains A,C and P68871 (HBB\\_HUMAN) mapped to "
"chains B,D."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:129 2b360ed21efe4eef94c513e47c7178e2
msgid ""
"``pdb_id`` (string) (required) PDB identifier (4-character code). "
"Examples: '4hhb' (hemoglobin), '1cbs' (CRABP2), '6lu7' (SARS-CoV-2 main "
"protease)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:146 52b31d3b7c5e4cb2bc8921de0428355c
msgid "**PDBe_get_uniprot_structure_coverage** (Type: BaseRESTTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:148 4db4226e10734b1aa57920547fff6950
msgid ""
"Get all PDB structures mapped to a UniProt protein, ranked by quality and"
" coverage, from the PDBe..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst 0e0af70a3f01424190cc761542ea94a7
msgid "PDBe_get_uniprot_structure_coverage tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:154 362009f3360541d3af921e4f679aaee7
msgid "**Name**: ``PDBe_get_uniprot_structure_coverage``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:156 e665a2fd60914fdfb9521a0bba82ccc1
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get all PDB structures mapped to a UniProt protein, "
"ranked by quality and coverage, from the PDBe Graph API. For each "
"structure, shows residue coverage on the UniProt sequence, resolution, "
"experimental method, mutations present, and ligands bound. Returns the "
"best chain per PDB entry. Essential for finding the best structural "
"coverage for a protein of interest and identifying which regions have "
"experimental structures vs predicted models. Example: P04637 (TP53) "
"returns 100+ structures covering different domains (DNA-binding domain "
"93-292, tetramerization domain 319-360, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_graph_tools.rst:160 b7bd6915204544409afed700082419d8
msgid ""
"``uniprot_id`` (string) (required) UniProt accession. Examples: 'P04637' "
"(TP53, many structures), 'P00533' (EGFR), 'P69905' (hemoglobin alpha), "
"'P01308' (insulin)."
msgstr ""

